### =========================================================================
### Lab 2: API Request Queries for Screenshots
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000
###
### Make sure the server is running first: npm run dev
### If you have the "REST Client" VS Code extension installed,
### you can simply click "Send Request" above any query!
### =========================================================================


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 1: get-all-books.png
### Route: GET /books/
### Description: Fetches all books from the database.
### Expected Status: 200 OK
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:3000/books/


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 2: get-single-book.png
### Route: GET /books/1/
### Description: Fetches a single book with ID = 1.
### Expected Status: 200 OK
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:3000/books/1/


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 3: post-book.png
### Route: POST /books/
### Description: Creates a new book record.
### Expected Status: 201 Created
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clean Code",
  "author": "Robert C. Martin",
  "price": 550,
  "pages": 464
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 4: put-book.png
### Route: PUT /books/1/
### Description: Updates the book details for ID = 1.
### Expected Status: 200 OK
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Atomic Habits (Updated Edition)",
  "author": "James Clear",
  "price": 499,
  "pages": 330
}


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 5: delete-book.png
### Route: DELETE /books/1/
### Description: Deletes the book with ID = 1.
### Expected Status: 200 OK
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/1/


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SCREENSHOT 6: error-not-found.png
### Route: GET /books/999/
### Description: Queries a non-existent book ID to test 404 error handling.
### Expected Status: 404 Not Found
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET http://localhost:3000/books/999/


